2B. Student KAFKA-TO- Student BDI SWITCHING ALGORITHM
---------------------------------------------------------------------

PURPOSE
Move event/data updates from the current Kafka-based path to BDI with a controlled cutoff, verification, and recovery plan.

STEP 1 — PLAN THE CUTOFF
  - Ask the BDI team for constraints, cutoff timing, dependencies, and preferred window.
  - If flexible and no blocking dependencies exist, tentatively target a date in November 2026, before the relevant deadline, leaving time for remediation.
  - Confirm stakeholders, change approvals, communication plan, monitoring owner, and freeze/cutover window.
  - The final date/time is NOT yet agreed.

STEP 2 — PRE-SWITCH READINESS
  - Confirm Task 1 backfill has been rehearsed and executed as required, and Task 2C reconciliation meets agreed gates.
  - Back up impacted SQL Server tables and verify recoverability.
  - Coordinate an additional database-level backup with the DBA where feasible.
  - Record Kafka offsets/checkpoints, BDI starting boundary, and exact cutover timestamp.
  - Define whether Kafka writes are paused, drained, or disabled before enabling BDI to avoid dual writes.
  - Verify BDI connector, credentials, scheduler, monitoring, schema and mapping readiness.
  - Establish a tested rollback procedure and an explicit rollback decision owner.

STEP 3 — CONTROLLED HANDOFF
  - Record the final Kafka processed boundary and verify outstanding Kafka events are drained or replayable.
  - Stop or disable Kafka updates according to the approved plan.
  - Enable BDI processing from the agreed boundary using the next-run start-time rule where applicable.
  - Prevent gaps and duplicate updates through checkpointing and idempotent processing.
  - For BDI-created or truly changed rows, set source = 'BDI'. Do not mass-update all source values merely because the source system changed.

STEP 4 — POST-SWITCH VALIDATION
  - Compare BDI event ingestion, database row counts, spot checks, source flags, and latency against expected behavior.
  - Run application smoke/regression tests and inspect errors, delayed events, and data anomalies.
  - Document outcome and obtain sign-off.

STEP 5 — FAILURE / ROLLBACK
  - If critical validation fails, stop new BDI processing safely; identify its last committed checkpoint.
  - Follow the approved restart/rollback plan to avoid data loss or double application.
  - Restore tables/database only after assessing any valid post-cutover writes that would otherwise be lost.
  - Escalate to BDI, DBA, application, and business owners; record incident and replan.

SWITCH FLOW
BDI Cutoff Discussion -> Agree Window -> Readiness & Mapping/Reconciliation Gates
 -> Verify Backups + Checkpoints + Rollback
 -> Disable/Drain Kafka -> Activate BDI -> Monitor & Reconcile
 -> PASS: Sign-off | FAIL: Contain, Recover, and Replan.

